{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('../logs/b9ef5b7f02d846a69d49a1aafc6ab7b7/stdout.log'):\n d=json.loads(line);o=d.get('Output','')\n if 'CA_EVENT' in o or 'rejected vote' in o or 'became candidate' in o: print(o.strip())\nPY\nsed -n '65,130p' ../submissions/8a18f0ee96e6421994f8ad58891db3ea/inputs/witness_explore_test.go\nsed -n '375,385p' ../agent-source/internal/raft/raft.go\nsed -n '1538,1566p' ../agent-source/internal/raft/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"2026-10-07 21:14:31.940038 W | raft: [f:1,l:2,t:1,c:2,a:2] [00001:00001] t2 became candidate\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"committed\",\"full2_last\":4,\"index\":5,\"run\":\"witness-recovery\",\"term\":2,\"witness_payload_bytes\":0,\"witness_type\":\"MetadataEntry\"}\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940623 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t3 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940688 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t3 rejected vote n00002 index4 term3,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940735 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t4 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940789 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t4 rejected vote n00002 index4 term4,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940829 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t5 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940881 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t5 rejected vote n00002 index4 term5,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940920 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t6 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.940972 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t6 rejected vote n00002 index4 term6,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.941025 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t7 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.941090 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t7 rejected vote n00002 index4 term7,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.941137 W | raft: [f:1,l:4,t:2,c:4,a:4] [00001:00002] t8 became candidate\n2026-10-07 21:14:31.941189 W | raft: [f:1,l:5,t:2,c:5,a:5] [00001:00003] t8 rejected vote n00002 index4 term8,logterm2,granttrue,utdfalse\nCA_EVENT {\"dropped\":8,\"event\":\"bounded_suffix\",\"full2_last\":4,\"full2_state\":\"Candidate\",\"full2_term\":8,\"run\":\"witness-recovery\",\"ticks_each\":100,\"vote_rejections\":6,\"witness_last\":5,\"witness_state\":\"Witness\",\"witness_term\":8}\n steps := 0\n pump := func(initial []pb.Message) {\n  queue := append([]pb.Message(nil), initial...)\n  for len(queue)>0 {\n   steps++\n   if steps>10000 { t.Fatal(\"message bound\") }\n   m:=queue[0]; queue=queue[1:]\n   if (phase==\"lag-full\" && m.To==2 && m.From==1) || (phase==\"leader-down\" && (m.To==1 || m.From==1)) { dropped++; continue }\n   if phase==\"leader-down\" && m.Type==pb.RequestVoteResp && m.From==3 && m.Reject { rejections++ }\n   nodes[m.To].p.Handle(m)\n   queue=append(queue,collect(m.To)...)\n  }\n }\n for i:=0;i<30 && nodes[1].p.raft.state!=leader;i++ { nodes[1].p.Tick();pump(collect(1)) }\n if nodes[1].p.raft.state!=leader || !nodes[1].p.raft.hasCommittedEntryAtCurrentTerm() { t.Fatal(\"election failed\") }\n // Commit and apply a real membership change before joining witness traffic.\n nodes[1].p.ProposeConfigChange(pb.ConfigChange{Type:pb.AddWitness,NodeID:3,Address:\"n3:1234\"},1)\n pump(collect(1))\n for i:=0;i<5;i++ {nodes[1].p.Tick();pump(collect(1))}\n for id:=uint64(1);id<=3;id++ {\n  if len(nodes[id].p.raft.remotes)!=2 || len(nodes[id].p.raft.witnesses)!=1 {t.Fatal(\"membership not established\")}\n  if nodes[id].p.raft.log.committed!=nodes[1].p.raft.log.committed {t.Fatal(\"join not caught up\")}\n }\n before:=nodes[1].p.raft.log.committed\n phase=\"lag-full\"\n nodes[1].p.ProposeEntries([]pb.Entry{{Type:pb.ApplicationEntry,Cmd:[]byte(\"payload\")}})\n pump(collect(1))\n idx:=nodes[1].p.raft.log.committed\n if idx!=before+1 || nodes[2].p.raft.log.lastIndex()!=before || nodes[3].p.raft.log.committed!=idx {t.Fatal(\"asymmetric commitment premise missing\")}\n ents,err:=nodes[3].p.raft.log.entries(idx,1024)\n if err!=nil || len(ents)!=1 {t.Fatal(\"witness entry not observed\")}\n emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"committed\",\"index\":idx,\"full2_last\":nodes[2].p.raft.log.lastIndex(),\"witness_type\":ents[0].Type.String(),\"witness_payload_bytes\":len(ents[0].Cmd),\"term\":nodes[1].p.raft.term})\n phase=\"leader-down\"\n for i:=0;i<100;i++ {\n  nodes[2].p.Tick();pump(collect(2))\n  nodes[3].p.Tick();pump(collect(3))\n }\n emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"bounded_suffix\",\"ticks_each\":100,\"full2_state\":nodes[2].p.raft.state.String(),\"witness_state\":nodes[3].p.raft.state.String(),\"vote_rejections\":rejections,\"full2_last\":nodes[2].p.raft.log.lastIndex(),\"witness_last\":nodes[3].p.raft.log.lastIndex(),\"full2_term\":nodes[2].p.raft.term,\"witness_term\":nodes[3].p.raft.term,\"dropped\":dropped})\n}\n\treturn len(r.remotes) + len(r.witnesses)\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) quorum() int {\n\treturn r.numVotingMembers()/2 + 1\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) isSingleNodeQuorum() bool {\n\treturn r.quorum() == 1\n}\n\n\t} else {\n\t\tplog.Debugf(\"%s is leader, ignored Election\", r.describe())\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) handleNodeRequestVote(m pb.Message) {\n\tresp := pb.Message{\n\t\tTo:   m.From,\n\t\tType: pb.RequestVoteResp,\n\t}\n\t// 3rd paragraph section 5.2 of the raft paper\n\tcanGrant := r.canGrantVote(m)\n\t// 2nd paragraph section 5.4 of the raft paper\n\tisUpToDate := r.log.upToDate(m.LogIndex, m.LogTerm)\n\tif canGrant && isUpToDate {\n\t\tplog.Warningf(\"%s cast vote from %s index %d term %d, log term: %d\",\n\t\t\tr.describe(), NodeID(m.From), m.LogIndex, m.Term, m.LogTerm)\n\t\tr.electionTick = 0\n\t\tr.vote = m.From\n\t} else {\n\t\tplog.Warningf(\"%s rejected vote %s index%d term%d,logterm%d,grant%v,utd%v\",\n\t\t\tr.describe(), NodeID(m.From), m.LogIndex, m.Term,\n\t\t\tm.LogTerm, canGrant, isUpToDate)\n\t\tresp.Reject = true\n\t}\n\tr.send(resp)\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) handleNodeConfigChange(m pb.Message) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration completed. The leader committed index 5 using the witness while the other full voter remained at index 4. With the leader unreachable, the connected survivor pair exchanged six rejected election attempts over 100 ticks; the witness rejected the stale log. This establishes bounded behavior, not an infinite stall or deadline violation. Whether this witness configuration owes the advertised majority-availability guarantee remains unresolved."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-replicate':\n  b['important_branches']=['Witness replication transforms non-configuration entries into MetadataEntry with term/index but no command payload; witnesses still contribute match values to the commit quorum.']\n  b['source_ids']+=['src-witness-metadata','src-witness-tests']\n if b['id']=='B-authority':\n  b['unknowns'].append('Whether the generic majority-availability statement applies after commitment by a full leader and witness while the remaining full voter lacks the entry; witness-specific availability scope is unresolved.')\n  b['source_ids']+=['src-witness-api','src-witness-config','src-majority-availability']\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='witness metadata commitment and successor election',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-replicate','B-authority'],reason='Witness metadata participates in commitment and vote freshness while witnesses cannot campaign or provide application payload. Generic majority availability versus witness-specific responsibility remains unresolved.',source_ids=['src-witness-api','src-witness-config','src-majority-availability','src-witness-metadata','src-term-election','src-log-safety'],high_consequence=True))\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Witness-backed commitment can leave the remaining full voter behind the witness metadata; election freshness protection then constrains acquisition of authority. Applicability of majority-availability language to this configuration remains open.')\nobs={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']+m['facts']}\nfor k in ['formation','context','connection']:\n p=m['core_overview'][k];p['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(p['source_ids']+[s for i in p['behavior_ids']+p['fact_ids'] for s in obs[i]['source_ids']]))\njson.dump(m,open('audit-map-witness.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='Which progress responsibility applies when a full leader and a metadata-only witness commit an entry, the other full voter lacks that entry, and the leader becomes unreachable: is majority availability owed to the connected full-voter/witness pair or restricted by an explicit witness fault contract?',importance='Potential loss of write availability with a majority of voting nodes connected. Vote rejection protects committed-history safety; bypassing freshness would not be a valid repair. Whether the implementation owes continuation in this witness configuration is unresolved.',participants=['Full leader','Lagging full voter','Witness voter'],objects=['Committed entry','Witness MetadataEntry','RequestVote/RequestVoteResp'],contexts=['Two full voters plus one witness added by committed configuration change','Leader becomes unreachable after asymmetric replication','Surviving pair remains connected'],event_paths=['ProposeConfigChange(AddWitness) -> apply -> catch-up','ProposeEntries -> leader/witness commit with full-voter delivery loss','Leader unreachable -> lagging full voter campaigns -> witness freshness rejection'],activity_classes=['A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B-replicate','B-authority'],fact_ids=['F-committed'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-membership':'Real witness admission and voting eligibility','B-persist':'Saved log metadata and update ordering in the no-crash exploration'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Witness support is explicitly experimental and has no application payload/state machine.','Vote log-freshness rejection protects the committed entry from replacement; observed rejection is not itself a defect.','No numeric progress deadline or explicit full-replica availability requirement was found in inspected witness interfaces.','Restoring the leader could permit catch-up, but that is outside the explored survivor-only fault interval.'],unknowns=['Does generic NodeHost majority availability include witness configurations with only one reachable complete copy at commit time, or does a more specific deployment/fault contract restrict it?','Is any implementation-owned recovery mechanism available to the surviving pair without the missing command payload? Current source shows witness cannot campaign/promote, but alternate deployment recovery duties are not exhausted.'],priority=2,trigger_rationale='A legal witness-add exploration reached committed index 5 with full voter 2 at index 4 and witness 3 holding a payload-free metadata entry. Subsequent source-consistent vote rejections expose a real premise of the broad availability statement; investigate the contract rather than invent a deadline or weaken freshness.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='source_review')\nq['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(['src-majority-availability','src-witness-api','src-witness-config','src-witness-metadata','src-witness-tests']+[s for i in q['behavior_ids']+q['fact_ids']+list(q['supporting_behavior_ids']) for s in obs[i]['source_ids']]))\nchanges={}\nfor i,ss,why in [('B-replicate',['src-witness-metadata','src-witness-tests'],'Clarify existing witness support is metadata support, not payload replication.'),('B-authority',['src-witness-api','src-witness-config','src-majority-availability'],'Retain a newly investigated applicability premise connecting witness metadata with election eligibility.'),('core_overview',['src-witness-metadata','src-term-election'],'Add the witness metadata/authority connection as an open local detail; the existing backbone is unchanged.')]:changes[i]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=ss,rationale=why,preserves='The confirmed read-context requirement concerns stable ordinary voters and the unchanged remote publication branch; no requirement, dependency or observation of that check is altered.')\np=dict(action='continue',map_path='audit-map-witness.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,rationale='Register the sourced witness availability premise without presuming an obligation or reclassifying exploratory observations as evidence.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b9ef5b7f02d846a69d49a1aafc6ab7b7','B-replicate','B-authority','F-committed','src-witness-api','src-witness-config','src-majority-availability','src-witness-metadata','src-term-election','src-log-safety'],answered='Exploration b9ef5b7f02d846a69d49a1aafc6ab7b7 exited zero. Its retained input launches two full voters, elects leader 1, commits/applies AddWitness(3), and checks membership and catch-up on all participants. It then drops leader-to-full-voter-2 messages for a proposal: raw committed event reports index=5, term=2, full2_last=4, witness_type=MetadataEntry and witness_payload_bytes=0. During the leader-unreachable suffix, the driver ticks nodes 2 and 3 100 times each and delivers their generated messages. Raw output records six RequestVoteResp rejections and full voter 2 ending Candidate at term 8/log index 4, witness 3 at term 8/index 5. Logs explicitly show grant=true but upToDate=false. This excludes the explanation that the ordinary voting/replication path automatically supplies a new leader during that finite suffix. It does not prove infinite stalling: terms and randomized timers change, and no repeatable full-state suffix or normative deadline is established. The driver substitutes no-crash persistence and a minimal Raft-level apply sink; it does not measure NodeHost application/client completion. Vote rejection is protective counterevidence, not something to disable. The new Candidate asks what progress scope the implementation actually owes.',remaining=['Investigate the witness-specific fault/deployment contract against the generic majority-availability statement.','Only if a responsibility is grounded, fix a new formal check and execute it; this exploration cannot be retro